    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Settled as Roman federates in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garonne">Garonne</a> valley in 418, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euric">Euric</a> (466–484) took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> Tarraconensis, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arles">Arles</a> and Marseille and were recognized as an independent kingdom by Julius Nepos in 475.</li><li>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaric-ii">Alaric II</a> fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> at Vouillé in 507 the kingdom lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimania">Septimania</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liuvigild">Liuvigild</a> conquered the Suebi in 585 and Swinthila drove the last Byzantine garrisons from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> by 625.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigothic-code">Liber Iudiciorum</a> of 654 gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> and Hispano-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> one law, based almost wholly on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a>, and became the basis of Spanish law through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> founded the only new cities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-europe">Western Europe</a> between the 5th and 8th centuries: Reccopolis, built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liuvigild">Liuvigild</a> in 578 with a palace and a mint after a victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>, Victoriacum, Luceo and Ologicus, raised with Basque labour in 621.</p></aside>
    </section>

