ulouse">Toulouse</a> becomes their capital.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">451</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-i">Theodoric I</a> fights under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Flavius Aetius</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains">Battle of the Catalaunian Plains</a> and is killed as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> are driven back.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">475</span><span class="rf-text">Julius Nepos signs an alliance granting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euric">Euric</a> the lands south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> and west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhone</a>; the kingdom is formally independent.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">507</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundians">Burgundians</a> kill <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaric-ii">Alaric II</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vouille">Battle of Campus Vogladensis</a> (Vouillé) and sack <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>; by 508 only <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimania">Septimania</a> remains in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">589</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reccared-i">Reccared I</a> renounces <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arianism">Arianism</a> at the Third Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> and the kingdom becomes Nicene Christian.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">625</span><span class="rf-text">Swinthila captures the last Byzantine holdings in <a class="enc-link" href="/en